# the funnel's diagonal guides: split cells, the floor's half inside, a wall's half outside (SPEC.md 130.24.4)
floor half left tile 31 15  flat 21.5
wall  half right tile 31 15  flat 23.5
floor half up tile 31 17  flat 21.5
wall  half down tile 31 17  flat 23.5
# the hump run's two humps: ridges across its 3 rows (the hump course's back hump's kind, SPEC.md 130.44)
hump 15 15 29 along y 3 open height 8
hump 21 15 29 along y 3 open height 8
# the BOOSTER chute's pads (SPEC.md 130.40)
prop boost 33 16 face +x strength 40
prop boost 34 16 face +x strength 40
prop boost 35 16 face +x strength 40
# the split: a pad at each exit (no archways: a rubber ball that hops one dies on what follows)
pad steel 51 18
pad glass 49 19
# steel: SPIKES across the only path (SPEC.md 130.38), a WATER column 3 deep, out of its front ARCH
prop spikes 53 17 55 20
water rect 56 17 57 20 top 14 bed 11
arch 56 19 +y
# glass: the MEMBRANE bridge, thin (glass-only, SPEC.md 130.38), and the LIFT (SPEC.md 130.12.6.4)
prop membrane 49 21 50 26
prop platform 46 27 4
# glass's maze (rev 9): its strands membrane, the FLOAT pool (water, no arch), the far bank's BOOST
prop membrane 35 27 40 28
prop membrane 33 23 34 26
prop membrane 30 27 32 28
water rect 24 26 29 29 top 18 bed 15
prop boost 22 28 face +y strength 40
# steel's MOMENTUM: a ridge hump across its 3-wide path, 8 px (11 stopped the slow steel ball)
hump 56 27 11 along x 3 open height 8

goal  rect 55 31 60 33  flat 11   # the steel finish
goal  rect 33 31 35 37  flat 10 exit 1   # the glass finish
start 8 7
checkpoint 30 16 ball rubber   # flag 0
checkpoint 49 16 ball rubber   # flag 1
checkpoint 48 27 ball glass   # flag 2
checkpoint 42 27 ball glass   # flag 3
checkpoint 33 27 ball glass   # flag 4
checkpoint 22 27 ball glass   # flag 5

